# VORRAT – SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE & UI/UX RULES

You are an expert full-stack developer working on the Vorrat pantry and cooking assistant app.
You must adhere strictly to these architecture and design rules for every single modification:

## 1. Design System & Styling
- Palette: Calm Nordic Culinary.
  - Primary: Forest green (`#2d5a3e` / `#059669`), soft mint background (`#ebf3ee` / `#ecfdf5`), border (`#c6dcce`).
  - Neutrals: Background `#f8fafc`, Cards `#ffffff`, Borders `#e2e8f0` / `#cbd5e1`, Primary text `#0f172a`, Secondary text `#64748b`.
  - Semantic warnings (SPARINGLY!): Amber (`#d97706` / `#fef3c7`) for soon expiring / partial stock. Red (`#dc2626` / `#fee2e2`) ONLY for expired, missing mandatory ingredient, or destructive delete actions.
- No visual experiments:
  - Max 2 badge colors per card header.
  - Same-row buttons MUST share identical height (32px or 36px), border-radius (8px or 10px), and flex centering.
  - Never squeeze status boxes into single-line flexboxes causing text truncation like `Hähnc...`. Secondary info must be placed on a tranquil second line.

## 2. Component Architecture & Code Organization
- Single Source of Truth:
  - Pantry Matching & Synonyms: ONLY via `src/utils/pantryMatching.ts` (`findMatchingPantryItem`, `getRecipePantryBreakdown`). No ad-hoc string comparisons in UI components.
  - Expiration & Warnings: ONLY via `isItemExpiringSoonOrCritical(item)`. Never count spices, sauces, or low piece counts without MHD.
  - Recipe helpers & categories: ONLY via `src/utils/recipeHelpers.ts`.
  - Storage keys: ONLY via `src/constants/storage.ts` (`STORAGE_KEYS`).
- Modals (`*Modal.tsx`):
  - Must close immediately on backdrop click, `✕` button (min 36x36px), and `Escape` key.
  - Never initialize modals to open (`true`) on initial app load.

## 3. Strict AI, API & Domain Rules
- FORBIDDEN: Fake or mock data.
  - NEVER generate or inject static dummy recipes ("Cremige One-Pot Pasta...") when an API call or scraper fails. Show clean, honest error UI.
  - NEVER invent hallucinated video or web URLs (`example.com`, fake YouTube IDs).
- Gemini API & Proxy:
  - All AI calls route through `callGeminiProxy`.
  - Allowed model cascade: `["gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "gemini-3.8-flash", "gemini-flash-latest", "gemini-flash-lite-latest"]`. Never use deprecated `gemini-2.0-flash` or `gemini-2.5-flash`.
- Ingredient Domain Logic:
  - Fresh vegetables (`Gemüse`, `Stk.`, `g >= 80`, `Bund`) must NEVER match spices (`Gewürz`, `Pulver`, `TL`, `Prise`).
  - Spices in recipes must always be individual items, never combined strings like "Salz & Pfeffer".

## 4. Definition of Done
Every task MUST pass before completion:
1. `npx tsc --noEmit` (0 errors)
2. `npm test` (All tests green)
3. Zero temporary test/debug scripts left behind.
